mission "Three Flags at Dusk"
    name "Three Flags at Dusk"
    description "Attend a secret parley between rival commanders before the expedition's trail becomes a new war."
    source "Lantern Bay"
    destination "San Telmo"
    reward 1265
    speaker offer "Admiral Vale"
    speaker visit "Admiral Vale"
    speaker complete "Admiral Vale"
    to offer
        has "The Convoy That Never Arrived: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The meeting place is a quiet quay at dusk. Three commanders have agreed to attend under separate flags, and none has brought more than a handful of guards.`
            `Admiral Vale watches the three sets of colours above the quay. "The expedition's trail has brought old enemies into the same harbour. If they leave believing the others are hiding something, we may have another war before we learn what happened."`
            choice
                `"Fair enough. Give me a heading and I will sail."`
                    accept
                `"What would happen if we leave it alone?"`
                    goto details
                `"I have my own course to keep. Find another ship."`
                    close
            label details
                `Vale sets the sealed papers on the table. "You will be the neutral hand here. Listen, carry the papers, and keep the captains talking long enough to compare what each one knows. No one leaves with a private version of the story."`
                choice
                    `"That settles it. Let us be about it."`
                        accept
                    `"I cannot take this on. Find another captain."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted Three Flags at Dusk. Attend a secret parley between rival commanders before the expedition's trail becomes a new war."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At San Telmo, Vale brings the three parties to the table. The evidence points to a place deliberately removed from the charts, not a treasure cache. "We have spent years arguing over flags," Vale says. "Now we must agree on what the papers actually say."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `The admiral watches the commanders depart. "They have agreed to continue the inquiry without bringing their fleets into it. That is not peace, not yet. But it is a better beginning than another line of broadsides."`
        log "Completed Three Flags at Dusk. Received 1265 gold. Attend a secret parley between rival commanders before the expedition's trail becomes a new war."
